<!--- Help page for the administration of Users --->

<table cellpadding=4 cellspacing=2 class="border" width="100%">
<tr>
	<td colspan="2"><strong>Low Risk</strong> </td>
</tr>
<!--- Risk Level 1 --->
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">1.</td>	
	<td class="border" valign="top">Award Fees & Incentive Fees are estimated and recorded as a percentage of costs incurred or revenue recognized and by definition not funded until the award fee/incentive fee modification is issued
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">2.</td>	
	<td class="border" valign="top">Modification Pending (Incremental Funding) applies where the customer only needs to provide incremental funding within the existing period of performance and contract ceiling. Mission Technologies has submitted a valid notice (i.e., 75% Letter/Limitation of Funds/Cost Notice) and/or Mission Technologies has been in communication with the contracts point of contact. 
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">3.</td>	
	<td class="border" valign="top">A modification is needed for additional period of performance where there is sufficient funding/ceiling for the period requested. 4. Letter Contracts and ATPs without a NTE Amount and/or authorization to bill that will not be definitized within 30 days will require an ARA/RI
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p></p>	
<table cellpadding=4 cellspacing=2 class="border" width="100%">
<tr>
	<td colspan="2"><strong>Medium Risk</strong> </td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">1.</td>	
	<td class="border" valign="top">Contractual Modification Pending applies where the customer needs to increase funding and extend period of performance. Mission Technologies has submitted a valid notice (i.e., 75% Letter/Limitation of Funds/Cost Notice) and/or Mission Technologies has been in communication with the contracts point of contact. </td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">2.</td>	
	<td class="border" valign="top">Change in SOW for an existing contract may include changes in contract value, funding, and/or period of performance. A change in scope can be triggered by a Mission Technologies’ submitted proposal requesting a change in contract scope or a requested technical change prior to written contractual notice. </td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">3.</td>	
	<td class="border" valign="top">Previous RI experience with customer resulted in difficulty clearing an RI or RI experience with the customer where the risk was not being cleared. </td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">4.</td>	
	<td class="border" valign="top">Any additional information that would cause concern with clearing an RI. </td>
</tr>
</table>
<p></p>	
<table cellpadding=4 cellspacing=2 class="border" width="100%">
<tr>
	<td colspan="2"><strong>Pre-Contract Cost (High Risk)</strong> </td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">1.</td>	
	<td class="border" valign="top">Pre-Contract/Production Costs for Cost Type contracts to include T&M contracts involved with working in advance of receiving a Binding Contract Agreement or if contract does not contain FAR 52.232-22, Limitation of Funds. Pre-contract costs are any costs incurred before the effective date of the contract or prior to receipt of customer’s authorization for pre-incurrence that were required to be incurred to meet schedule or another qualifying circumstance for a contract requirement. To be allowable an advanced agreement with the customer is necessary. </td>
</tr>
</table>